.Dd October 25, 2026
.Dt MIDNIGHTBSD-SYSTEM-MONITOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm midnightbsd-system-monitor
.Nd display system processes, resources, and mounted file systems
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
opens a GTK 3 window with four tabs.
Processes lists process IDs, owners, states, CPU use, and resident memory.
Selecting a process enables End Process, which sends
.Dv SIGTERM ,
and Force Quit, which sends
.Dv SIGKILL ;
both are also available from the row's context menu and ask for
confirmation first.
Process names, mount points, and device strings are shown with control and
bidirectional formatting characters replaced so a row cannot disguise itself.
Resources graphs total CPU use, physical memory use, and aggregate network
receive and transmit rates.
File Systems lists mounted file systems with capacity, used space, and
space available to ordinary users.
Hardware summarizes the CPU, installed memory, swap allocation and use,
OS release, and physical drives.
Drive types use reported rotation rates
when available; optical drives and NVMe drives are identified by device type.
The Refresh hardware button updates this summary after hardware changes.
Processes and resources refresh every two seconds; file systems refresh
every ten seconds.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr midnight-wm 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Lucas Holt
